-- An ASSUMEd predicate that carries a TYPICALLY. It becomes an input predicate
-- the Blawx interview asks about, so the default is dropped, and the export has
-- to say so (R-TYPICALLY). The older spelling is used on purpose: a section GIVEN
-- with a scalar default has no category subject and is refused by Blawx before
-- it could carry anything.
DECLARE Person IS ONE OF alice, bob

GIVEN p IS A Person
ASSUME `is authorised` p IS A BOOLEAN TYPICALLY TRUE

@export May enter
GIVEN q IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`may enter` q MEANS `is authorised` q
